# Git and repository standards

Apply on **every** Hollow Crown project and when the user starts or reorganizes a GitHub repo.

## Commits

- Use **Conventional Commits**: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `build`, `chore`, `remove`.
- Optional scope: module or area, e.g. `feat(hub): ...`.
- **One logical change per commit** (additions, removals, refactors not mixed arbitrarily).
- Update `CHANGELOG.md` under `## [Unreleased]` for user-visible changes.
- Call out **removals** and **breaking changes** explicitly.

## New or reorganized repos

1. Add `README.md`, `.gitignore`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md` when the project is non-trivial.
2. Document layout in `docs/REPO_LAYOUT.md` (or README section) before the tree grows ad hoc.
3. **Commit after each logical unit of work** — not one giant commit at the end.
4. Do **not** run `git config --global`; use repo-local `-c user.name=...` or env vars if identity is missing.

## Hollow Crown Platform monorepo

- Root: `HC-Platform` — Hub stack only.
- Paths: `api/`, `foundation/`, `hub/`, `minigames/<game>/`.
- New Hub minigames go under `minigames/` and root `pom.xml` `<modules>`.
- Server deploy: **three** JARs (Foundation, Hub, minigame) — not one uber-JAR. See `docs/PACKAGING.md`.

## When editing

- Match existing module boundaries; do not add unrelated files to the same commit.
- After structural moves, commit with `refactor:` or `chore:` and note path changes in CHANGELOG.
